    "title": "Sacramento Kings at Charlotte Hornets: Odds, Injury Updates, How to Watch and More",
    "text": "Date: March 24, 2026Time: 7 p.m. ETVenue: Spectrum CenterTV: FDSSEStreaming: Check local listingsRadio: 610 AM, Sports 1140 KHTKBuy tickets: Buy Kings at Hornets tickets on StubHubThe Kings have enjoyed a four-game homestand but will soon have to dust off their road jerseys. They will head out to take on the Charlotte Hornets at 7:00 p.m. on Tuesday at Spectrum Center. The Kings must know they'll be fighting an uphill battle given the 17-point spread they're up against.AdvertisementThe away team had wound up with the win the last three times the Kings and the Nets have met, but the home crowd finally got their W on Sunday. The Kings snuck past the Nets with a 126-122 win.The Kings' success was spearheaded by the efforts of Malik Monk, who went 7-for-13 from beyond the arc en route to 32 points and 6 assists, and Maxime Raynaud, who dropped a double-double with 22 points and 10 rebounds. As a matter of fact, that's the most points Monk has scored all season.The Kings were looking sharp from deep and finished the game having made 14 of their 27 three-pointers. That's their best three-point shooting percentage since January 12th.AdvertisementMeanwhile, the Hornets waltzed into their game on Saturday with two straight wins...and they left with three. They put the hurt on Memphis with a sharp 124-101 victory. Charlotte was heavily favored coming into this contest, and the results showcase why.The Hornets' win was the result of several impressive offensive performances. One of the most notable came from LaMelo Ball, who posted 29 points and 3 steals. Brandon Miller was another key player, shooting 66.7% (8-12) from the field on his way to 22 points and 5 rebounds.Charlotte has now won five of their last six games at home. That's provided a massive bump to their 37-34 record this season. The wins were due in large part to their defensive effort, having only surrendered 104.8 points on average over those games. As for Sacramento, their victory bumped their record up to 19-53.AdvertisementSacramento Kings at Charlotte Hornets Odds, Line and SpreadBetting lines as of 03/24/2026 at 9:28 AM ET. Odds subject to change.Moneyline (ML): Hornets -1639 | Kings +906Against the spread (ATS): Hornets -17 (-110) | Kings +17 (-110)Over/Under (O/U): 229.5 (O: -110 | U: -110)Sacramento Kings Injury ReportDrew Eubanks (Thumb) - Out for the SeasonDomantas Sabonis (Back) - Out for the SeasonPrecious Achiuwa (Back) - day-to-dayIsaiah Stevens (Ankle) - day-to-dayKeegan Murray (Ankle) - outDe'Andre Hunter (Eye) - Out for the SeasonDaeqwon Plowden (Foot) - day-to-dayKillian Hayes (Toe) - day-to-dayNique Clifford (Foot) - outZach LaVine (Finger) - Out for the SeasonCharlotte Hornets Injury ReportKon Knueppel (Back) - day-to-dayTidjane Salaün (Calf) - outKings vs. Hornets: Schedule ImpactKings: Playing on normal rest (1 day off). Record in this situation this season: 9-34SAC: lost 16 of last 18 games with regular restHornets: Playing on long rest (2 days). Record in this situation this season: 7-10Kings vs. Hornets: Head-to-Head in 2025-26 SeasonCharlotte Hornets lead the season series 1-0Kings vs. Hornets: AnalysisWhy the Kings Can Win: CHA: 1-6 ATS in last 7 games against the Western Conference at homeWhy the Hornets Can Win: CHA: covered 3 straight games as the favoriteAdvertisementDisclosure: Some or all of this content may have been generated by AI. While we strive for accuracy, AI can occasionally produce incorrect information. If you buy something via one of our links, we may earn a commission.This story was originally published by Athlon Sports on Mar 24, 2026, where it first appeared in the NBA section. Add Athlon Sports as a Preferred Source by clicking here.",
